across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Thunnus is a genus of ocean-dwelling, ray-finned bony fish from the mackerel family, Scombridae. More specifically, Thunnus is one of five genera which make up the tribe Thunnini – a tribe that is collectively known as the tunas. Also called the true tunas or real tunas, Thunnus consists of eight species of tuna (more than half of the overall tribe), divided into two subgenera."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-thunnus"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunnus"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine",[["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"]]],["Soviet cuisine","cuisine/soviet-cuisine",[["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"]]],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Canned fish","ingredient/canned-fish"],["Canning","ingredient/canning"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Grated cheese","ingredient/grated-cheese"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]}]},"ingredient/dashi":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/dashi","n":"Dashi","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 3 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Dashi is a family of stocks used in Japanese cuisine. Dashi forms the base for miso soup, clear broth soup, noodle broth soup, and many simmering liquids to accentuate the savory flavor known as umami. Dashi is also mixed into the flour base of some grilled foods like okonomiyaki and takoyaki."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-dashi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dashi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Japanese cuis